## Materials
ILs, $\mathrm{{C_{12}m i m C l}}$ (purity $599\%$ ), $\mathrm{BmimBF_{4}}$ (purity> $99\%$ ), BmimOTf (purity> $599\%$ ), ${\mathrm{BmimPF}}_{6}$ (purity $599\%$ ) and $\mathrm{BmimClO_{4}}$ (purity $599\%$ ) were purchased from the Centre of Green 55 Chemistry and Catalysis, LICP, CAS. Organic salts $\mathrm{TBABF}_{4}$ (purity $599\%$ ) and ${\mathrm{TBAPF}}_{6}$ (purity> $99\%$ ) were also obtained from this company. $\mathrm{\ZnCl}_{2}$ (A. R. grade), KCl (A. R. grade), ${\mathrm{K}}_{3}{\mathrm{Fe}}({\mathrm{CN}})_{6}$ (A. R. grade), glycerol (A. R. grade), acetonitrile (A. R. grade), methanol (A. R. grade), DMF(A. R. grade), metal foils 60 (Au, Ag, Pt, Fe, Zn and $\mathrm{Cu}$ , purity ${>}99.99\%$ ) were provided by Sinopharm Chemical Reagent Co., Ltd, P. R. China. 1,3,5- Benzenetricarboxylic acid $\mathrm{(H_{3}B T C}$ , purity> $99\%$ ) were obtained from J & K Scientific Ltd. Toray Carbon Paper (CP, TGP-H-60, $19\times19~\mathrm{cm}$ ) and Nafion N-117 membrane ( $0.180\mathrm{mm}$ thick, $\geq0.90$ 65 $\mathrm{meg/g}$ exchange capacity) were purchased from Alfa Aesar China Co., Ltd. Before used, the ILs were dried in vacuum oven at 80 $^{\mathrm{{o}}}\mathrm{{C}}$ for 48 hrs and the water content was less than $0.1~\mathrm{wt\%}$ as determined by Karl-Fischer method.25
## Zn-MOFs synthesis
70 The procedures to synthesize the $Z\mathrm{n}$ -MOFs were similar to that reported previously.26 In a typical experiment, $\mathrm{15~\:g}$ $\mathrm{C_{12}m i m C l}$ , $_{\mathrm{~5~g~}}$ glycerol, desired amount of $\mathrm{\ZnCl}_{2}$ and $\mathbf{0.8\textrm{g}}$ $\mathrm{H}_{3}\mathrm{BTC}$ were added into a two-necked round-bottomed flask, and the mixture was stirred vigorously at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $72~\mathrm{{hrs}}$ . After the 75 reaction, the obtained mixture containing the materials was mixed with $50~\mathrm{mL}$ ethanol and then centrifuged with a speed of 5000 rpm. The obtained $Z\mathrm{n}$ -MOFs were washed with ethanol for 10 times and dried in a vacuum oven at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $24~\mathrm{{hrs}}$ .
## SAXS study
80 SAXS experiments were carried out at Beamline 1W2A at the Beijing Synchrotron Radiation Facility. The apparatus and the procedures were similar to that used in previous work.15c The data were collected using a CCD detector (MAR) with maximum resolution of $3450\times3450$ pixels. The wavelength of the X-ray was $_{85}~1.54\mathrm{~\AA~}$ , and the distance of the sample to detector was $1.31~\mathrm{m}.$ . In a typical experiment, the sample was added into the sample cell, and the $\mathrm{\DeltaX}$ -ray scattering data were recorded. The 2-D SAXS images were obtained from the detector and then transformed into the profiles of intensity (I) vs wavevector $(q)$ by the software $^{90}$ FiT2D. The pair-distance distribution function $p({\mathfrak{r}})$ was obtained
